  "slug": "common-cli-flags",
  "title": "Common CLI flags, and where macOS differs",
  "skills": ["tooling", "terminal"],
  "difficulty": "intro",
  "estimatedMinutes": 15,
  "objectives": [
    "Recall what each letter means in `ls -la`, `rm -rf`, `grep -rniE`, `cp -a`, `mkdir -p`, `tail -F` and `ps aux`",
    "Guard `rm -rf` against an empty variable with `${VAR:?}`, and put `--` before an operand that starts with `-`",
    "Find the process listening on a port with `lsof -ti tcp:PORT -sTCP:LISTEN`, and stop it with `kill` before reaching for `kill -9`",
    "Spot the macOS (BSD) vs GNU differences that break scripts: `sed -i ''`, `date -v`, `cp -R src/`, `find` without a path, `xargs` on empty input, `readlink -f`, `timeout`"
  ],
